# Node Engine — Dataflow runtime

Lives in **`packages/runtime/src/node-engine/`** (the `@effects/runtime` package). Depends on **PixiJS only** — no React/MUI/@xyflow/react. The supplier app and any future Tier-3 runtime consume this verbatim.

> **Engine knows nothing about pages or clones.** Multi-page UI and viewer-only clone aliases (`PipelineNodeData.cloneOf`) live in `apps/editor/`. UI calls `sceneResolver.resolveSceneForEngine(pages)` before pushing edges — dedupes real nodes, rewrites clone-source edges to point at the original. The engine sees a flat `(real nodes, resolved edges)` view. `engine.setEdges` / `engine.addNode` / `engine.removeNode` are the **single boundary**. Don't introduce engine-side awareness of pages/clones — use UI-side resolvers. Supplier app skips multi-page entirely and feeds `engine.addNode` / `engine.setEdges` directly from `pipeline.graph.nodes / .edges`.

