## Core types

### `SLOT` enum

```
TEXTURE | NUMBER | VEC | CONFIG | CONTOUR
EVENT   | SIGNAL | ANIMATION
METRICS | TEXT   | TEXT_STYLE
ANY     // wildcard, only on type-erased handles
```

`SLOT_COMPAT` lives in `apps/editor/src/components/node-editor/constants.ts`. `ANY` accepts every type. No `POLYGON` slot (geometry → `CONTOUR`); no `DEPTH_RAW` slot (depth processors retired).

### Signal interfaces

```ts
EventSignal     { count, lastTimestampMs, lastX?, lastY? }
Signal          { value, time, age, state: 0|1, lastTimestampMs }
ChannelSignal   { time, raw, value, state: 0|1 }     // time = unclamped drive (NOT Signal.time ms)
AnimationSignal { channels: Record<string, ChannelSignal> }
TextStyle       { font, letterSpacing, weight, transform }
EffectMetrics   { effectName, totalMs, cpuMs, gpuDispatchMs, passes: PassMetric[], timestampMs }
ContourSamples  { version: 1, closed, count, totalLength, aabb: [4], positions, tangents, arcS }
```

`ChannelSignal.time` carries the unclamped drive value so a paused Timer freezes the channel — see `animation-system.mdc`.

### `ProcessorDef`

```ts
{
  type: string                   // unique key, also React Flow node type
  title: string
  category: 'input' | 'animTrigger' | 'animMod' | 'animCtrl'
          | 'imageOp' | 'contour' | 'output' | 'util'
          | 'depth' | 'ai' | 'source' | 'process' | 'marigold' | 'dnf'  // legacy
  inputs: HandleDef[]            // { name, type, label? }
  outputs: HandleDef[]
  defaultParams: Record<string, unknown>
  hidden?: boolean               // hidden from "Add Node" picker; still loadable from snapshot
}
```

Legacy categories tolerated for snapshot back-compat — don't remove without a migration.

### `IDataflowEngine` (what processors see)

Narrow facade: `app`, `defaultWidth/Height`, `renderPass`, `renderPassInto`, `markDirty`, `getOutputs`. Processors call only these. `DataflowEngine` exposes more (`addNode`, `subscribeNode`, etc.) — that surface is editor-only.

## Lifecycle

1. `new DataflowEngine(app)` — takes a hidden offscreen Pixi `Application`.
2. `addNode(id, type, initialParams?)` — instantiate from `PROCESSOR_CATALOG[type]`, store params, mark dirty, `rebuildGraph()`.
3. `setEdges(edges)` — rebuild adjacency + Kahn's topo sort, mark all dirty.
4. `start()` — kick rAF loop.
5. `tick()` per accepted frame: mark `alwaysDirty` → bail if dirty empty → walk topo order, gather inputs, run `execute()`, store in `outputCache`, notify subscribers → clear dirty set.
6. `stop()` / `destroy()` — release rAF, destroy processors, clear maps + `nodeListeners`.

### FPS gate (`setTargetFps(fps)`)

`0` = uncapped (native rAF). Positive throttles `tick()` to ~`1000/fps` ms with 0.5 ms slack (60fps cap doesn't drop alternate frames to 30fps from rAF jitter). Only graph evaluation gated; rAF still composites the last frame so static scenes don't stutter.

Persisted by toolbar to `localStorage["nodeEditor.fps.v1"]`, re-applied by `usePipelineEngine`.

### Dirty propagation (`markDirty(nodeId)`)

BFS over adjacency from `nodeId`, marking all reachable descendants. Triggers:
- `updateNodeParams`.
- `setEdges` / `addNode` / `removeNode` (structural change marks **everything** dirty).
- Async observers — `eventEmitter` on emit, `image` after load, `segmentation` on SAM result, `textStrip` on rasterise, etc.
- Implicitly every frame for `alwaysDirty` processors.

### `alwaysDirty` processors

`effect`, `eventEmitter`, `tapZone`, `timer`, `envelope`, `combineSignals`, `signalSwitch`, `animationController`, `animationSwitch`. Reasons: clock-owners, external-event reactors, per-frame compositors. `interpolator` and `log` are intentionally NOT alwaysDirty (pure / dependent on upstream propagation). `noiseVisualizer` likewise — frozen when no upstream Signal is wired.

### Subscriber preservation across snapshots

`engine.subscribeNode(id, cb)` keys listeners by **node id**, not by processor instance. `applySnapshot` (undo/redo, scene import) tears down + immediately re-adds nodes with the same ids; React views stay mounted with stable `[engine, id]` deps.

Therefore `removeNode` MUST NOT drop `nodeListeners.get(id)` — rebuilt processors would publish into an empty Set and previews/metrics/output-readers freeze on the pre-undo frame. The unsubscribe closure deletes the empty Set entry once the last listener detaches, so permanently-removed nodes don't leak. **Never reintroduce `nodeListeners.delete(id)` inside `removeNode`** — the historical "previews freeze after undo" bug.

`destroy()` does clear `nodeListeners` (entire engine going away).

### Topological execution

Kahn's algorithm. Cycles can be wired (React Flow doesn't reject up front), but `rebuildGraph` only enqueues `inDegree === 0` nodes — anything in a cycle never executes. Connect-time cycle detection lives in `apps/editor/.../wouldCreateCycle` (UI side); engine itself doesn't validate.

### Input gathering

`gatherInputs(nodeId)` reads `outputCache[source][sourceHandle]` per incoming edge into `inputs[targetHandle]`. Missing source output → `inputs[handle]` is undefined; processors must tolerate.

## GPU helpers

- `renderPass(fragment, resources, w?, h?) → RenderTexture` — fullscreen quad `Mesh` via `Shader.from({ gl: { vertex: DEFAULT_VERTEX, fragment }, resources })`, render into a fresh `RenderTexture(w×h, scaleMode=linear)`. Caller owns the RT.
- `renderPassInto(target, fragment, resources)` — same, into a caller-owned RT (recycled by `BaseProcessor.ensure*RT`).
- Geometry cached per `(w, h)` in `geoCache`. Destroyed in `engine.destroy()`.

`DEFAULT_VERTEX` lives in `packages/runtime/src/pipeline/default-vertex.ts` (Pixi v8 `uProjectionMatrix * uWorldTransformMatrix * uTransformMatrix`).

## `BaseProcessor` contract

### Required

- `readonly def: ProcessorDef`.
- `execute(inputs, params, engine) → Record<string, any>` — pure of mutable state but free to mutate it. Returns a flat record stored in `outputCache`.

### Optional

- `alwaysDirty: boolean`.
- `nodeId: string` — engine writes this on `addNode`. Use for `engine.markDirty(this.nodeId)` from async callbacks.

### Helpers

- `val(inputs, params, key, fallback)` — priority `inputs[key] > params[key] > fallback`.
- `resolveRes(inputs, params, engine) → [w, h]`:
  1. Explicit `width`/`height` (input or param) when both > 0.
  2. `source` input dimensions.
  3. `sdf` input dimensions.
  4. Any other texture-like input dimensions.
  5. `engine.defaultWidth × engine.defaultHeight` (900×1200).

  Stops a small auxiliary texture (e.g. 512×512 atlas) from accidentally driving canvas resolution.
- `ensureRT(w, h)` / `ensurePing(w, h)` / `ensurePong(w, h)` — RT pool of size 1/1/1 per processor. Recreates on dimension change, destroys old. Use this — never `RenderTexture.create` directly (per-frame allocation drowns the GPU).
- `destroy()` — destroys the three RTs. Override and call `super.destroy()` to release additional resources (workers, cached coord textures, sprite display objects).

### Texture ownership

- A processor's output `texture` slot publishes a Pixi `TextureSource` (e.g. `rt.source`), **not** a `Texture` wrapper. Downstream nodes that need a `Texture` create a one-shot wrapper and **destroy it**. Canonical pattern: single reused wrapper recreated only when the upstream source identity changes (see `Preview` and `Segmentation`). Allocating a fresh `Texture` per frame became multi-GB tab usage in the past.
- Source ownership stays with the producer. Consumers don't destroy `inputs.<x>`.
- The `image` processor unloads the previous URL via `Assets.unload(prevUrl)` before reloading (otherwise `Assets` cache holds the prior bitmap forever).

## Adding a new processor — checklist

1. `packages/runtime/src/node-engine/processors/<name>.ts`: export `<name>Def: ProcessorDef` and `class <Name>Processor extends BaseProcessor` with `def` + `execute`. Set `alwaysDirty = true` for clock/external-event nodes. Override `destroy()` to release auxiliary resources.
2. Register in `processors/index.ts → PROCESSOR_CATALOG`.
3. Build a view `apps/editor/src/components/flow-nodes/views/<Name>NodeView.tsx` (uses `BaseNodeShell` + widgets from `@effects/ui`).
4. Register in `apps/editor/.../flow-nodes/nodeTypes.ts → pipelineNodeTypes`.
5. Add to `apps/editor/.../node-editor/menuGroups.ts → RAW_GROUPS` under the right section (also drives picker accent colour).
6. If supplier-relevant (whole-node exposure or accepts `data.exposed.fields`), update `publish-plane.mdc → Classify reached nodes` and consider adding a custom widget in `apps/supplier/`.
7. New SLOT type → extend `SLOT` + `SLOT_COMPAT`; document in `project-overview.mdc` and `product-vision.mdc`.
8. Add a section to `processors-catalogue.mdc`.

## Pitfalls

- Returning a fresh object reference every frame from an `alwaysDirty` processor is fine for the engine but expensive for React subscribers. Gate publication or memoise inside the view if the value rarely changes.
- Wrong field for animation drive: shaders bind `uChan{i}.x` (drive, unclamped) by default. `.y` is clamped 0..1, `.z` is `lerp(min, max, raw)`, `.w` is state.
- Reading `Signal.time` instead of `Signal.value` — `time` keeps growing whenever the Timer runs (paused intervals skipped) and ignores Interpolator/Combine reshaping. Always drive from `value`.
- Forgetting `engine.markDirty(this.nodeId)` at the end of an async callback (image load, SAM reply, text rasterisation) — engine has no way to learn the state changed; new outputs only surface on the next unrelated propagation.
